{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"snowwhite-cryptozoic-duiker","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Why\nEvery prompt/detector change in this epic must be measured, or we repeat dso's mistake of\nuncalibrated drift. This is the gating foundation: no prompt story merges without a passing eval.\n\n## What\nBuild eval specs for the four-pass code-review prompts (base, overlays, verify) in the existing\nrebar eval harness. Seed two families from dso's documented corpus:\n- NO-FIRE cases (must not flag): sourced-bash functions, subdirectory scripts, list-form subprocess,\n  Rule-5 structural greps on declarative artifacts, moved-code renames with callers updated,\n  already-public config reads, valid observable-postcondition tests.\n- SEEDED-DEFECT recall cases (must flag): tautological test, dangling deletion, asymmetric signature\n  change, hallucinated API, VCS conflict marker, ticket scope drift.\nDeterministic gating scorers (a deterministic scorer GATES; an llm-judge only REPORTS).\n\n## Scope\nEval specs + fixtures under src/rebar/llm/evals and eval_specs; no gate behavior change here.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Eval specs exist for base, verify, and at least the tests+security overlays.\n- [ ] No-fire and recall case families seeded from the dso incidents listed above.\n- [ ] At least one deterministic gating scorer per spec; specs pass on the current gate as baseline.\n- [ ] The nit-framing experiment result (positive-framing recall lift) captured as a case.","id":"de7c-323a-05e4-4fda","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Eval foundation for the four-pass code-review prompts"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788220351011415001,"uuid":"a6fbf7e1-1856-4d8b-9601-6c06e31f4d33"}